  "note": "Independent re-judgment after 381e927417, which changed RIBManager.dumpRIBForMRT's per-route callback dispatch. The MRT snapshot is not passing a path to other BGP peers, and that commit changed neither reconstructWireAttrs (whose AggregatorFlags, CommunityFlags, ExtCommunityFlags and LargeCommunityFlags carry a received Partial bit) nor appendOtherAttrsWireForMRT. 562bc0139d changed no UPDATE path. The other units on the stale list changed in other commits (writeUpdateBody in 735771cf03, negotiated family admission on raw UPDATE writes; rib_recovery, rib_structured, storage/routeentry.go) and add no negative. The verdict stays weak for its recorded reason: every tag on RFC4271-5-4 is positive, the row has neither a negative test nor a {single-polarity} annotation (./le rfc check reports \"has no negative test\"), so for this MUST NOT no test feeds the violating case (a recognized transitive optional attribute received with Partial 1) and observes Ze refusing to clear it as distinct from a path that never clears any flag. The positive covers listed in the tests map remain as the prior verdict describes them.",
